# Production settings + the D2 replay overlay (lane D2-DATA): rank 0 saves the taps rows and input ids of requests tagged
# d2r.<seq>.<from>.<end> (d2/replay.py sets request_id) into ~/dsv41-offload-run/d2-replay/<seq>/ on sparkhead.
# Not a benchmark configuration: tagged requests copy their rows to the host and write them to disk.
# Before start_exp on BOTH nodes, as the host user: mkdir -p ~/dsv41-offload-run/d2-replay  (a docker-created mount
# point is root-owned and the files would be unreadable to the copy). Model: A (local DSpark drafter), so the overlay's
# DSparkSpeculator.propose is the one the engine calls; taps come from the target alone, whatever the drafter.
LABEL=A-replay
OVERLAYS="offload/dspark/capture/speculator_replay.py=/usr/local/lib/python3.12/dist-packages/vllm/v1/worker/gpu/spec_decode/dspark/speculator.py"
EXTRA_DOCKER_ARGS="-v \$HOME/dsv41-offload-run/d2-replay:/d2-replay"
EXP_DOCKER_ENV="VLLM_DSPARK_REPLAY_DIR=/d2-replay VLLM_DSPARK_REPLAY_SYNC_MB=256"
